/**
\page page_sttriggerdata2005 StTriggerData2005

\brief Concrete StTriggerData implementation for STAR Run 5 (year 2005) trigger data.

\section sec2005_overview Overview

StTriggerData2005 is the concrete implementation of the StTriggerData abstract interface for
<b>STAR Run 5 (year 2005)</b> raw trigger data.  It wraps a \c TrgDataType2005 structure and
exposes its content through the common StTriggerData accessor API.

Compared to StTriggerData2004, Run 5 introduces access to <b>Level-2 algorithm trigger
results</b> through L2ResultsOffset() and isL2Triggered(), reflecting the activation of online
L2 triggers during the Cu+Cu run.

\section sec2005_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
StObject
  └── StTriggerData          (abstract interface)
        └── StTriggerData2005
\endcode

\section sec2005_runyear Run Year
Run 5, calendar year 2005 &mdash; Cu+Cu collisions at &radic;s = 200 GeV.

\section sec2005_datamembers Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| mData  | TrgDataType2005* | Pointer to the raw Run 5 trigger bank in memory. |

\section sec2005_new New Compared to 2004

- L2ResultsOffset(StL2AlgorithmId id) &mdash; byte offset for a given L2 algorithm in the
  L2 results block.
- isL2Triggered(StL2TriggerResultType id) &mdash; returns \c true if the specified L2 trigger
  result type is set.

getDsm0_BEMCE(), getDsm0_BEMCW(), and getDsm1_BEMC() return \c nullptr for this format.

\section sec2005_usage Usage Example
\code{.cpp}
StEvent* event = static_cast<StEvent*>(GetInputDS("StEvent"));
const StTriggerData* trgData = event->triggerData();
if (trgData) {
    bool l2ht = trgData->isL2Triggered(L2TriggerResultType_BEmcHighTower);
    unsigned short zdcSum = trgData->zdcHardwareSum(0);
}
\endcode

\see StTriggerData
\see StTriggerData2004
\see StTriggerData2007
*/
